ds or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":213419,"global_rank":259068},{"name":"kennygao/cellular-automata","owner":"kennygao","html_url":"https://github.com/kennygao/cellular-automata","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213419,"global_rank":259079},{"name":"andrewnachtigal/Algorithms","owner":"andrewnachtigal","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewnachtigal/Algorithms","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Python implementation of algorithms. Self study materials to accompany MIT OCW 6.006","topics":[],"score":213416,"global_rank":259086},{"name":"meetapandit/python-oo-practice","owner":"meetapandit","html_url":"https://github.com/meetapandit/python-oo-practice","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"repo to share practice problems on OOP in Python","topics":[],"score":213411,"global_rank":259112},{"name":"nishitde/Data-Dictionary","owner":"nishitde","html_url":"https://github.com/nishitde/Data-Dictionary","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213405,"global_rank":259119},{"name":"sripathi-muralitharan/Major-Project-2018-19","owner":"sripathi-muralitharan","html_url":"https://github.com/sripathi-muralitharan/Major-Project-2018-19","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A repository for the major project","topics":[],"score":213402,"global_rank":259133},{"name":"pcodes/md-deeplens-sensor-identifier","owner":"pcodes","html_url